# A load that fails leaves no current file, so every query after it would
# check the file again and fail the same way -- a full re-check per
# question.  While the file on disk is still the one that failed, a query
# is answered with that load's error from memory instead, and the error's
# data says so.
{"method":"load","params":{"file":"%FILE%"}}
{"method":"goals"}
{"method":"goal","params":{"goal":0}}
# An explicit reload checks again regardless.
{"method":"reload"}
# The first edit clears the memory: the query reloads, and the goals are
# back.
!edit wrong = not ==> wrong = not true
{"method":"goals"}
# Only the edit above may have touched the file.
!unchanged
{"method":"close"}
